JWasm: -Zj writes an absolute public in a 16-bit PUBDEF if it fits

MASM 5 writes a public constant in a 16-bit PUBDEF record if its value
fits in 16 bits, signed (-32768 to 32767) or unsigned (up to 65535), as
the comment in omf_write_pubdef describes. JWasm wrote negative values
in a 32-bit PUBDEF (91h), which wlink then takes as FFFFFFFFh.

Needed for DISKCOPY, whose FINE EQU -1 is PUBLIC (DISKCOPY.EQU) and
used by DCOPYPAR.ASM as EXTRN FINE:ABS.

diff --git a/src/omf.c b/src/omf.c
index da7bf0d..6389afc 100644
--- a/src/omf.c
+++ b/src/omf.c
@@ -1432,7 +1432,11 @@ static ret_code omf_write_pubdef( void )
              * JWasm behaves differently, resulting in negative values to be stored as 32-bit.
              */
 #if 1
-            is32 = ( sym->offset > 0xffffUL ? 1 : 0 );
+            /* -Zj: like Masm 5, which writes FINE EQU -1 (DISKCOPY) as FFFFh */
+            if ( Options.masm5_compat )
+                is32 = ( (int_32)sym->offset > 0xffff || (int_32)sym->offset < -32768 ? 1 : 0 );
+            else
+                is32 = ( sym->offset > 0xffffUL ? 1 : 0 );
 #else
             is32 = ( sym->offset > 0xffff || sym->offset < -32768 ? 1 : 0 ); /* this is what Masm does */
 #endif
